Game-Terminal-Kit

The part of a terminal game that is the same in every terminal game: reading
one key at a time and naming it, drawing a frame without flicker, leaving
colour out when it is not wanted, and giving the terminal back on every way
out. The games started by the game command are built on it.

INSTALLATION

To install this module, run the following commands:

	perl Makefile.PL
	make
	make test
	make install

SUPPORT AND DOCUMENTATION

After installing, you can find documentation for this module with the
perldoc command.

    perldoc Game::Terminal::Kit

You can also look for information at:

    RT, CPAN's request tracker (report bugs here)
        https://rt.cpan.org/NoAuth/Bugs.html?Dist=Game-Terminal-Kit

    Search CPAN
        https://metacpan.org/release/Game-Terminal-Kit


